--- the documentation of the limitation (installed source, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-beam-sharp/c0642514-f9d1-5f22-91e2-015f96c1f119/scratchpad/env/lib/erlang/lib/tools-4.1.4/src/xref.erl)
    40	_Unresolved calls_{: #unresolved_call } are calls to `apply` or
    41	`spawn` with variable module, variable function, or variable
    42	arguments. Examples are `M:F(a)`, [`apply(M, f, [a])`](`apply/3`), and
    43	[`spawn(m, f(), Args)`](`spawn/3`). Unresolved calls are represented
    44	by calls where variable modules have been replaced with the atom
    45	`'$M_EXPR'`, variable functions have been replaced with the atom
    46	`'$F_EXPR'`, and variable number of arguments have been replaced with
    47	the number `-1`. The above mentioned examples are represented by calls
    48	to `'$M_EXPR':'$F_EXPR'/1`, `'$M_EXPR':f/1`, and `m:'$F_EXPR'/-1`. The
    49	unresolved calls are a subset of the external calls.
    50	
    51	> #### Warning {: .warning }
    52	>
    53	> Unresolved calls make module data incomplete, which implies that the results
    54	> of analyses may be invalid.
    55	
